From a7b79fdbd6fdf3e671e982d77b5cfb664cd804f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Message-Id: <a7b79fdbd6fdf3e671e982d77b5cfb664cd804f6.1782842988.git.thorsten.klein@bshg.com>
From: Thorsten Klein <thorsten.klein@bshg.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 14:26:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Add read-only fallback cache directories

Add the read_only_dirs (CCACHE_READONLY_DIRS) config option for
specifying one or more additional local cache directories to use as
read-only fallback caches.

When a result is not found in the local cache_dir, the read-only
directories are searched in order. A hit is promoted (copied) into the
local cache, including any associated raw files, so subsequent lookups
are served locally. The read-only directories are never written to or
cleaned up.

This is useful in CI environments where an ephemeral writable cache can
be combined with one or more pre-populated caches, for example built
from the main or development branch.
